      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ef1f3c92",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man holding car keys while another person holds a glass of alcohol, with text questioning why alcohol is banned in Islamic countries but not in Western countries. The overall intent is to provoke a debate or challenge perceptions about cultural or religious norms regarding alcohol consumption. While not explicitly targeting any specific group with hate or abuse, the meme's framing can be seen as harmful because it oversimplifies complex cultural, religious, and legal contexts, potentially reinforcing stereotypes or misrepresenting the reasons behind bans in different societies. The juxtaposition of the car keys and alcohol may imply a critique of Western consumerism or moral relativism, but the message risks reducing nuanced cultural practices to a simplistic binary comparison, which can be misleading and contribute to misunderstanding between cultures.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_21f32587"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
