      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "alcohol as a symbol of prohibition in Islamic countries",
      "description": "The text 'if this is banned in islamic countries' maps onto the visual entity of the glass of alcohol, implying that alcohol is the subject of the ban in Islamic countries. The visual material (alcohol) is being referenced by the textual material to establish a context for comparison.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_21f32587"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_716424ec",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_2",
      "label": "car keys as a symbol of freedom or consumerism in Western countries",
      "description": "The text 'shouldn't this be banned in western countries?' maps onto the visual entity of the car keys, implying that the car keys represent a value or norm in Western countries that is being contrasted with the alcohol ban in Islamic countries. The visual material (car keys) is being referenced by the textual material to establish a counterpoint for the rhetorical question.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_21f32587"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b961acab",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the rhetorical question and implied comparison in the scene",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material and the scene as a whole, which frames the viewer as someone who must evaluate the moral or cultural equivalence between alcohol bans in Islamic countries and the permissiveness of alcohol in Western countries. The rhetorical question 'shouldn't this be banned in western countries?' implicitly addresses the user, inviting them to consider their own cultural stance or values. The user is not explicitly projected onto a specific visual material (like the man or the keys) but onto the conceptual contrast established by the scene and text, which requires the user to position themselves in relation to the cultural comparison.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_21f32587"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
